asr-001061
01:16:19.720 --> 01:16:25.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: what percentage of investigative resources is devoted to these priority cases?

asr-001062
01:16:25.020 --> 01:16:28.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: How many such cases were filed and resolved annually?

asr-001063
01:16:29.080 --> 01:16:33.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Doon sa mga high-ranking officials, grave offenses?

asr-001064
01:16:59.500 --> 01:17:13.140
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor, we will not be able to tally that, Your Honor,

asr-001065
01:17:13.220 --> 01:17:15.520
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: but we will submit, we will comply with the committee, Your Honor.

asr-001066
01:17:15.560 --> 01:17:17.320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay, we'll just wait for the submission.

asr-001067
01:17:18.100 --> 01:17:21.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Likewise, can you update the committee on how many officials were dismissed,

asr-001068
01:17:21.580 --> 01:17:23.860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: suspended, sama na rin siguro ito sa report,

asr-001069
01:17:24.320 --> 01:17:27.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: suspended, fined, reprimanded, or otherwise sanctioned?

asr-001070
01:17:27.660 --> 01:17:31.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: How many Ombudsman decisions were actually implemented by agencies?

asr-001071
01:17:32.120 --> 01:17:33.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So this is it.

asr-001072
01:17:33.760 --> 01:17:35.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Or how many were overturned?

asr-001073
01:17:35.240 --> 01:17:36.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Or modified or appealed?

asr-001074
01:17:36.320 --> 01:17:37.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Probably can include this also in the report.

asr-001075
01:17:37.800 --> 01:17:39.040
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We will submit that, Your Honor.

asr-001076
01:17:39.260 --> 01:17:40.240
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We will submit to the committee.

asr-001077
01:17:40.760 --> 01:17:46.040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And then, what avenues for participation are currently available for civil society organizations

asr-001078
01:17:46.040 --> 01:17:49.840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to participate in anti-corruption efforts of the Ombudsman?

asr-001079
01:17:52.000 --> 01:17:57.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: How can they participate, ang CSOs, mga civil society organizations and watchdogs?

asr-001080
01:17:58.340 --> 01:18:01.620
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: They can actually send us complaints, Your Honor, and we will investigate.

asr-001081
01:18:01.620 --> 01:18:05.680
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We will act with dispatch, with guides to these, with our, being sent to us.

asr-001082
01:18:06.520 --> 01:18:15.660
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Sometimes the expectation is too high that they will send a statement full of supposed facts,

asr-001083
01:18:16.060 --> 01:18:18.940
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: but nothing is supported by the statements.

asr-001084
01:18:19.520 --> 01:18:21.660
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: So it will be a little more complicated.

asr-001085
01:18:21.660 --> 01:18:26.420
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But if they can submit to us a more comprehensive statement on the wrongdoing,

asr-001086
01:18:26.800 --> 01:18:28.340
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: then we can act faster, Your Honor.

asr-001087
01:18:31.210 --> 01:18:33.090
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: There's a question from the media.

asr-001088
01:18:33.650 --> 01:18:37.010
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Bakit kailangan ng Ombudsman ng 54 million na confidential funds?

asr-001089
01:18:38.570 --> 01:18:42.910
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Nung panahon ni Martires, under 2024, 2025, 1 million lang daw,

asr-001090
01:18:43.250 --> 01:18:47.010
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: pero pinapa-realign in other items, no.

asr-001091
01:18:47.550 --> 01:18:49.390
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So it's from the media.

asr-001092
01:18:49.970 --> 01:18:55.920
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think we're more aggressive in pursuing investigations, Your Honor,

asr-001093
01:18:56.040 --> 01:19:03.300
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and purchasing information and other things that requires confidential funds to be utilized, Your Honor.

asr-001094
01:19:04.000 --> 01:19:04.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya pala natutulog noon.

asr-001095
01:19:06.440 --> 01:19:07.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sige, President Pro Tempore.

asr-001096
01:19:07.900 --> 01:19:09.900
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Mr. Chairman, that's it.

asr-001097
01:19:09.940 --> 01:19:15.240
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: A drop in the bucket kung tutuusin for what the work of the Ombudsman is doing.

asr-001098
01:19:15.680 --> 01:19:23.580
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: As a matter of fact, there was one office, one office of government that had 125 million five times,

asr-001099
01:19:24.100 --> 01:19:26.720
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: for confidential funds, hindi ba?

asr-001100
01:19:28.040 --> 01:19:33.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And definitely, as we mentioned, in these budget hearings,

asr-001101
01:19:33.400 --> 01:19:39.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: we will confine confidential funds

asr-001102
01:19:39.820 --> 01:19:46.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: only to law enforcement agencies, investigative agencies and those connected with national security.

asr-001103
01:19:46.820 --> 01:19:53.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And of course, the office of the Ombudsman, in its drive against corruption, will be one of them.

asr-001104
01:19:53.080 --> 01:19:59.320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And I think 54 million will be very much justified, no. Mababa na nga yun compared to 1 million noon.

asr-001105
01:19:59.320 --> 01:20:03.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya sabi ko nga hindi ko alam kung nagtatrabaho noon with 1 million,

asr-001106
01:20:03.100 --> 01:20:05.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: whatever ano kung mabibili noon.

asr-001107
01:20:05.100 --> 01:20:08.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Probably, our Senate President, you have some questions?

asr-001108
01:20:08.660 --> 01:20:09.660
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-001109
01:20:09.660 --> 01:20:20.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I do agree na yung 54 million is minuscule compared to the gravity of the corruption cases that we are embroiled in.

asr-001110
01:20:20.260 --> 01:20:25.860
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And the Ombudsman is tasked to resolve all of those corruption issues.

asr-001111
01:20:25.860 --> 01:20:34.760
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Admittedly, kailangan talaga ng legitimate purchase of information

asr-001112
01:20:34.760 --> 01:20:37.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: para ma-establish yung evidence,

asr-001113
01:20:37.500 --> 01:20:39.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: lalong lumakas yung kaso at makasuhan natin

asr-001114
01:20:39.660 --> 01:20:40.660
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: at manalo tayo sa pagkaso

asr-001115
01:20:40.660 --> 01:20:46.660
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kasi hindi lang mag-file ng cases kundi dapat manalo tayo doon sa mga kaso.

asr-001116
01:20:46.660 --> 01:20:56.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, I think the 51 million is well justified so that we can strengthen the cases that we

asr-001117
01:20:56.960 --> 01:20:57.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: will file.

asr-001118
01:20:57.960 --> 01:21:02.180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I have a few policy questions, Ombudsman.

asr-001119
01:21:02.180 --> 01:21:06.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: This is in relation to a topic that we're discussing here on the floor.

asr-001120
01:21:06.460 --> 01:21:07.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: yung barangay term setting.

asr-001121
01:21:07.460 --> 01:21:08.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: no?

asr-001123
01:21:09.460 --> 01:21:13.820
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And kayo, nag-local government rin kayo, Ombudsman.

asr-001124
01:21:13.820 --> 01:21:19.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: May plano kasi habaan yung term to five years.

asr-001125
01:21:19.700 --> 01:21:24.520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kung magaling yung kapitan, walang problema. Pero kung yung kapitan bulok, problema tayo.

asr-001126
01:21:24.520 --> 01:21:26.140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Lalo na kung corrupt.

asr-001127
01:21:26.140 --> 01:21:27.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Di ba, Tito Sen?

asr-001128
01:21:27.460 --> 01:21:30.560
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yun yung interpolation mo kahapon.

asr-001129
01:21:30.560 --> 01:21:36.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So I would like to pick your brains on your opinion on extending the five-year term.

asr-001130
01:21:36.460 --> 01:21:37.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And then what are the

asr-001131
01:21:37.460 --> 01:21:38.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: recourses

asr-001132
01:21:38.460 --> 01:21:44.120
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: that our constituents can go to, especially with the Ombudsman?

asr-001133
01:21:44.220 --> 01:21:49.880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kung may mga kapitan na hindi nagfa-function, hindi nagtatrabaho, corrupt, ano yung mga remedies nila?

asr-001134
01:21:50.820 --> 01:21:57.560
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor, the office of the ombudsman can dismiss barangay captains who do not do their job.

asr-001135
01:21:58.500 --> 01:22:03.920
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And I think all we need is a substantiated complaint, a complaint that people will stand up to,

asr-001136
01:22:03.920 --> 01:22:09.060
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: will try to prove to us so that we can utilize this power given to us by the law.

asr-001137
01:22:10.960 --> 01:22:15.340
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And it's just something, it's just probably unfortunate that I have to mention this.

asr-001138
01:22:16.220 --> 01:22:19.700
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Many of those that we have dismissed in the office of the ombudsman institutionally,

asr-001139
01:22:21.100 --> 01:22:26.200
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: in many cases, these are talking about many, many cases, were reversed by the Court of Appeals.

asr-001140
01:22:27.800 --> 01:22:32.180
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: That is a trend, Your Honor, that's known to the whole office of the ombudsman.

asr-001141
01:22:32.720 --> 01:22:33.900
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's something that...

asr-001142
01:22:33.920 --> 01:22:39.040
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: That I spoke about to Senior Associate Justice Marvic Leonen.

asr-001143
01:22:39.180 --> 01:22:40.980
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I told him about this problem that we have.

asr-001144
01:22:41.780 --> 01:22:48.460
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Because institutionally, it's very discouraging to be conducting all of these activities

asr-001145
01:22:48.460 --> 01:22:56.020
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: only to be reversed by the Court of Appeals decision that came out of nowhere.

asr-001146
01:22:56.180 --> 01:22:57.880
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I mean, sometimes we feel that way.

asr-001147
01:22:58.620 --> 01:23:03.120
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And I was actually confronted with that problem as Secretary of Justice

asr-001148
01:23:03.120 --> 01:23:03.520
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because...

asr-001149
01:23:03.920 --> 01:23:07.320
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: There was somebody dismissed by the office of the ombudsman

asr-001150
01:23:07.320 --> 01:23:10.280
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: who was...

asr-001151
01:23:10.280 --> 01:23:12.440
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Which decision was reversed by the Court of Appeals

asr-001152
01:23:12.440 --> 01:23:17.960
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and was trying to get back to his office in the NBI.

asr-001153
01:23:19.100 --> 01:23:23.300
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And I could not honor that kind of logic

asr-001154
01:23:23.300 --> 01:23:24.980
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because he had been dismissed already.

asr-001155
01:23:25.760 --> 01:23:30.000
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And if you will be reversed in your dismissal,

asr-001156
01:23:30.480 --> 01:23:32.100
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: what then is the power given to us?

asr-001157
01:23:32.100 --> 01:23:33.520
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: If that will be the case.

asr-001158
01:23:33.920 --> 01:23:37.400
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: So, that's one of the dilemmas that we face with the judiciary, Your Honor.

asr-001159
01:23:37.800 --> 01:23:39.980
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I'm sorry to say, but as a lawyer,

asr-001160
01:23:40.340 --> 01:23:45.000
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: it's not really common for lawyers to complain about the courts.

asr-001161
01:23:45.660 --> 01:23:48.060
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But sometimes we just have to raise that issue already

asr-001162
01:23:48.060 --> 01:23:53.040
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because it can be the biggest elephant in the room within our justice system.

asr-001163
01:23:53.420 --> 01:23:55.520
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: If you talk about foreign investment,

asr-001164
01:23:56.160 --> 01:23:58.620
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we have a problem with foreign investment

asr-001165
01:23:58.620 --> 01:24:03.560
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because there's no certainty that the rules will apply to the judiciary.

asr-001166
01:24:03.920 --> 01:24:07.960
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's something that has to be dealt with face-to-face by our people

asr-001167
01:24:07.960 --> 01:24:11.540
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and by the legislators, by all of us.

asr-001168
01:24:12.140 --> 01:24:14.880
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's the biggest elephant in the room for this country.

asr-001169
01:24:15.640 --> 01:24:20.360
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: The judiciary has to be examined closely by everybody in government

asr-001170
01:24:20.360 --> 01:24:22.920
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and they themselves should go on a soul-searching

asr-001171
01:24:22.920 --> 01:24:25.000
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: so that we can be a better country.

asr-001172
01:24:25.220 --> 01:24:27.580
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think that that's one of the problems besetting us right now.

asr-001173
01:24:29.770 --> 01:24:32.990
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ombudsman, I really appreciate your...

asr-001174
01:24:35.330 --> 01:24:39.390
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: being proactive instead of just waiting for cases to be filed

asr-001175
01:24:39.390 --> 01:24:40.510
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: and aaktuhan.

asr-001176
01:24:40.950 --> 01:24:43.350
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yung nakikita ko na proactive ngayon ang Ombudsman,

asr-001177
01:24:43.410 --> 01:24:48.930
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: meaning you go after the issues before it explodes,

asr-001178
01:24:49.110 --> 01:24:50.990
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: which is the right way to do.

asr-001179
01:24:51.670 --> 01:24:55.030
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: However, kagaya ng nasabi ng ating mga kasamahan,

asr-001180
01:24:55.250 --> 01:24:58.610
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: the wheels of justice, kasama dito ang judiciary.

asr-001181
01:24:59.490 --> 01:25:03.790
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kanina narinig ko sinabi niyo na it takes on average 15 years in the Sandiganbayan

asr-001182
01:25:03.790 --> 01:25:05.310
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: to resolve a case.

asr-001183
01:25:05.330 --> 01:25:12.050
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ngayon, the CA also reverses a lot of the decisions you make.

asr-001184
01:25:12.990 --> 01:25:14.850
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And I'm not blaming them.

asr-001185
01:25:15.170 --> 01:25:20.030
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I am just saying, yung wheels of justice putol eh.

asr-001186
01:25:20.230 --> 01:25:21.310
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Hindi gumugulong eh.

asr-001187
01:25:21.510 --> 01:25:22.410
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Parang na-stuck up siya.

asr-001188
01:25:23.010 --> 01:25:28.670
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So what efforts is the ombudsman doing together with the judiciary

asr-001189
01:25:28.670 --> 01:25:34.670
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: to resolve this turning of the will of justice

asr-001190
01:25:34.670 --> 01:25:35.310
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: to make it more effective?

asr-001191
01:25:35.330 --> 01:25:41.810
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: More efficient, faster, and also to make it just for our constituents?

asr-001192
01:25:42.110 --> 01:25:44.210
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasi kung ang Ombudsman proactive,

asr-001193
01:25:44.870 --> 01:25:45.830
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kabilang banda naman hindi,

asr-001194
01:25:46.830 --> 01:25:48.550
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: sayang, sayang yung efforts.

asr-001195
01:25:49.270 --> 01:25:55.430
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Well, that's something that I looked at when I was Secretary of Justice, Your Honor.

asr-001196
01:25:56.130 --> 01:25:57.830
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: When I was the Secretary of Justice,

asr-001197
01:25:57.970 --> 01:26:00.910
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we had this Justice Sector Coordinating Council,

asr-001198
01:26:00.910 --> 01:26:04.630
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: which involved the courts, the Department of Justice,

asr-001199
01:26:05.330 --> 01:26:07.650
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and the Department of Interior and Local Government

asr-001200
01:26:07.650 --> 01:26:09.990
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: so that we could coordinate our efforts.

asr-001201
01:26:10.890 --> 01:26:15.470
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But actually, that was a program sponsored by the European Union.

asr-001202
01:26:15.810 --> 01:26:17.810
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: They were the ones that funded that program.

asr-001203
01:26:18.470 --> 01:26:22.030
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Probably, we need one that will include the ombudsman, Your Honor,

asr-001204
01:26:22.630 --> 01:26:25.010
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: so that the wills of justice will grind faster.

asr-001205
01:26:25.810 --> 01:26:29.850
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And if you ask me, I mean, if we look back in history,

asr-001206
01:26:29.850 --> 01:26:33.750
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think I was in law school when EDSA happened.

asr-001207
01:26:33.750 --> 01:26:36.410
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And if there's one thing that was never touched

asr-001208
01:26:36.410 --> 01:26:40.850
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: with all the EDSAs that happened to this country,

asr-001209
01:26:41.210 --> 01:26:41.970
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: it's the judiciary.

asr-001210
01:26:42.990 --> 01:26:48.470
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Never has the judiciary accounted for everything that they've been doing.

asr-001211
01:26:49.210 --> 01:26:51.550
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It is something that we have to examine as a country.

asr-001212
01:26:52.150 --> 01:26:59.510
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Because when businessmen come in to invest and create jobs

asr-001213
01:26:59.510 --> 01:27:01.750
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and give progress to the country,

asr-001214
01:27:02.190 --> 01:27:03.710
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: when a case is thrown,

asr-001215
01:27:03.750 --> 01:27:06.410
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and a monkey wrench is thrown into the business,

asr-001216
01:27:06.710 --> 01:27:09.850
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: there's no certainty that the case will be finished

asr-001217
01:27:09.850 --> 01:27:11.210
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: within a certain amount of time.

asr-001218
01:27:11.770 --> 01:27:15.090
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It is something that has to be addressed also by our people,

asr-001219
01:27:15.310 --> 01:27:17.730
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: by the senior members of the Supreme Court

asr-001220
01:27:17.730 --> 01:27:21.570
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: about how fast can justice roll, the wills of justice roll.

asr-001221
01:27:22.370 --> 01:27:27.430
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's actually a problem that has been there for the longest time.

asr-001222
01:27:27.950 --> 01:27:30.210
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But it has to be said openly.

asr-001223
01:27:30.490 --> 01:27:32.110
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I'm daring to do this, Your Honor,

asr-001224
01:27:32.110 --> 01:27:33.650
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because I have no more.

asr-001225
01:27:33.750 --> 01:27:34.150
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I have no more aspirations.

asr-001226
01:27:34.450 --> 01:27:38.990
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: This is the job I want for myself and for the country

asr-001227
01:27:38.990 --> 01:27:41.050
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: to be able to finish this job, Your Honor.

asr-001228
01:27:41.730 --> 01:27:45.210
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And that's why things that have been left unsaid

asr-001229
01:27:45.210 --> 01:27:48.170
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: are being said now because it has to happen.

asr-001230
01:27:48.630 --> 01:27:51.770
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: If we're able to cure our justice system

asr-001231
01:27:51.770 --> 01:27:53.330
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and make it function properly,

asr-001232
01:27:53.750 --> 01:27:55.590
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we will be a much better country, Your Honor.

asr-001233
01:27:55.770 --> 01:27:57.530
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We will be a much, much better country.

asr-001234
01:27:58.670 --> 01:28:01.190
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: With your coordination, what's the feedback?

asr-001235
01:28:01.190 --> 01:28:02.650
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I heard you say na meron

asr-001236
01:28:02.650 --> 01:28:03.190
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: you have a...

asr-001237
01:28:03.750 --> 01:28:05.750
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Coordination or that committee.

asr-001238
01:28:06.430 --> 01:28:08.030
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Now, what's the feedback from the judiciary?

asr-001239
01:28:08.430 --> 01:28:08.770
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Are they all...

asr-001240
01:28:08.770 --> 01:28:11.110
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Well, I usually speak to my classmates.

asr-001241
01:28:11.210 --> 01:28:12.430
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I usually speak to my classmates,

asr-001242
01:28:12.790 --> 01:28:14.910
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Senior Associate Justice Marvic Leonen.

asr-001243
01:28:15.470 --> 01:28:18.190
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Of course, sometimes he questions me about speaking out

asr-001244
01:28:18.190 --> 01:28:20.090
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: about these things that I'm saying.

asr-001245
01:28:20.710 --> 01:28:21.730
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But it has to be said.

asr-001246
01:28:22.410 --> 01:28:23.790
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We cannot hold this back anymore.

asr-001247
01:28:24.010 --> 01:28:27.930
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I mean, how many times do you have in your life

asr-001248
01:28:27.930 --> 01:28:28.990
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: to serve as ombudsman

asr-001249
01:28:28.990 --> 01:28:32.930
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and give your critique of what's happening in society?

asr-001250
01:28:33.050 --> 01:28:33.630
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Because it is a role...

asr-001251
01:28:33.630 --> 01:28:34.790
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It is a role that was given to us.

asr-001252
01:28:36.030 --> 01:28:39.150
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's something that probably I may be cautioned,

asr-001253
01:28:39.190 --> 01:28:40.930
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: but the message arrives.

asr-001254
01:28:41.570 --> 01:28:46.130
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And I'm sure that I have distressed our Chief Justice

asr-001255
01:28:46.130 --> 01:28:47.770
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: many times with my remarks.

asr-001256
01:28:48.330 --> 01:28:49.330
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But it has to happen.

asr-001257
01:28:49.470 --> 01:28:50.710
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It has to be done, Your Honor.

asr-001258
01:28:51.070 --> 01:28:53.830
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I'm doing this at great risk probably to many lawyers.

asr-001259
01:28:54.370 --> 01:28:57.370
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: They will not even think about doing something like this.

asr-001260
01:28:57.710 --> 01:28:59.710
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But I think I've arrived at the point

asr-001261
01:28:59.710 --> 01:29:02.730
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: where this has to be said properly, Your Honor,

asr-001262
01:29:02.750 --> 01:29:03.450
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: in order to make it happen.

asr-001263
01:29:03.450 --> 01:29:04.950
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: In open court, in open session,

asr-001264
01:29:05.810 --> 01:29:10.550
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: so that people will know what ails us

asr-001265
01:29:10.550 --> 01:29:12.770
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and that there is a light at the end of the tunnel

asr-001266
01:29:12.770 --> 01:29:14.110
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: if we really look at it.

asr-001267
01:29:14.690 --> 01:29:16.070
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And that is one of them, Your Honor,

asr-001268
01:29:16.190 --> 01:29:17.730
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: is to be able to correct

asr-001269
01:29:17.730 --> 01:29:21.570
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and then make efficient the wheels of justice, Your Honor.

asr-001270
01:29:23.130 --> 01:29:24.870
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I support that, Ombudsman.

asr-001271
01:29:25.170 --> 01:29:31.670
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And like mga ano lang, in the ordinary day-to-day activities

asr-001272
01:29:32.350 --> 01:29:33.050
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: of our country,

asr-001273
01:29:33.450 --> 01:29:33.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: our constituents,

asr-001274
01:29:34.770 --> 01:29:36.670
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: especially in public service,

asr-001275
01:29:38.010 --> 01:29:39.850
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kagaya po sa mga kapitan,

asr-001276
01:29:40.590 --> 01:29:42.090
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: iyan diretso sa tao iyan.

asr-001277
01:29:42.830 --> 01:29:45.570
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And pag nagsumbong ang tao sa Ombudsman

asr-001278
01:29:45.570 --> 01:29:48.070
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: or sa ibang mga government agencies,

asr-001279
01:29:48.190 --> 01:29:50.970
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kung hindi nag-function yung accountability mechanism natin,

asr-001280
01:29:51.610 --> 01:29:55.230
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: when I say accountability, lahat ito,

asr-001281
01:29:55.410 --> 01:29:57.450
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: from the Ombudsman to the judiciary,

asr-001282
01:29:58.910 --> 01:29:59.450
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: hindi naman

asr-001283
01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:03.940
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: nadedehado yung respondent

asr-001284
01:30:03.940 --> 01:30:05.180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: o yung nakusahan.

asr-001285
01:30:05.180 --> 01:30:07.140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Nadedehado yung taong bayan.

asr-001286
01:30:07.540 --> 01:30:09.100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Sila ang nadedehado dito.

asr-001287
01:30:09.680 --> 01:30:11.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kaya I really support

asr-001288
01:30:11.260 --> 01:30:13.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: making our

asr-001289
01:30:13.620 --> 01:30:14.940
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: wills of justice efficient.

asr-001290
01:30:15.220 --> 01:30:17.340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And that's what hopefully we can

asr-001291
01:30:17.340 --> 01:30:19.360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: contribute

asr-001292
01:30:19.360 --> 01:30:21.040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: during the budget season.

asr-001293
01:30:21.460 --> 01:30:23.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In all aspects, in all agencies

asr-001294
01:30:23.420 --> 01:30:23.980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: as well.

asr-001295
01:30:25.080 --> 01:30:26.020
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Thank you, Your Honor.

asr-001296
01:30:26.420 --> 01:30:29.180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I have a few items in the budget

asr-001297
01:30:29.180 --> 01:30:31.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: that I want to ask.

asr-001298
01:30:33.200 --> 01:30:35.340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I asked this last year, but I

asr-001299
01:30:35.340 --> 01:30:37.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: saw an increase in

asr-001300
01:30:37.420 --> 01:30:39.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: the development and implementation

asr-001301
01:30:39.400 --> 01:30:41.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: of integrity promotion programs

asr-001302
01:30:41.740 --> 01:30:43.580
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: to generate a critical

asr-001303
01:30:43.580 --> 01:30:45.760
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: mass of anti-corruption advocates

asr-001304
01:30:45.760 --> 01:30:47.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: in the campaign against

asr-001305
01:30:47.600 --> 01:30:48.900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: official abuse.

asr-001306
01:30:49.520 --> 01:30:52.140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: From 44 million to 148

asr-001307
01:30:52.140 --> 01:30:52.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: million.

asr-001308
01:30:54.280 --> 01:30:55.540
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Can you give us

asr-001309
01:30:55.540 --> 01:30:58.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: a preview on

asr-001310
01:30:58.960 --> 01:31:00.900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: why this program

asr-001311
01:31:00.900 --> 01:31:02.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: increased? And I support this

asr-001312
01:31:02.440 --> 01:31:04.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: because obviously

asr-001313
01:31:04.200 --> 01:31:07.180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: fighting corruption

asr-001314
01:31:07.180 --> 01:31:09.180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: comes with promoting

asr-001315
01:31:09.180 --> 01:31:10.220
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: anti-corruption.

asr-001316
01:31:10.820 --> 01:31:12.920
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Making sure that if we can promote it

asr-001317
01:31:12.920 --> 01:31:14.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: to our students, it's better

asr-001318
01:31:14.460 --> 01:31:16.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: for them to know the consequences

asr-001319
01:31:17.600 --> 01:31:19.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: before they enter the government service.

asr-001320
01:31:20.000 --> 01:31:20.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And also

asr-001321
01:31:20.420 --> 01:31:22.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: the noble

asr-001322
01:31:22.480 --> 01:31:24.860
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: philosophy

asr-001323
01:31:24.860 --> 01:31:26.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: of going into public service.

asr-001324
01:31:26.480 --> 01:31:27.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, I just want to get

asr-001325
01:31:27.500 --> 01:31:28.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: feedback.

asr-001326
01:31:28.960 --> 01:31:30.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: On why this program increased

asr-001327
01:31:30.800 --> 01:31:32.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: by almost three-folds.

asr-001328
01:31:33.300 --> 01:31:35.660
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor, in the Ombudsman's office,

asr-001329
01:31:35.660 --> 01:31:36.860
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we have a small auditorium

asr-001330
01:31:37.540 --> 01:31:38.980
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: where we entertain

asr-001331
01:31:39.900 --> 01:31:42.000
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: students and advocates

asr-001332
01:31:42.000 --> 01:31:43.200
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: of good governance

asr-001333
01:31:43.840 --> 01:31:45.940
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: to give us a visit so that we can

asr-001334
01:31:45.940 --> 01:31:47.580
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: have a dialogue and they can observe

asr-001335
01:31:48.100 --> 01:31:49.620
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: the goings-on in our office.

asr-001336
01:31:50.220 --> 01:31:52.540
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And we deem this to be a very effective

asr-001337
01:31:52.540 --> 01:31:53.940
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: tool, Your Honor, especially

asr-001338
01:31:54.400 --> 01:31:56.100
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: with young people being brought in.

asr-001339
01:31:57.100 --> 01:31:58.960
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: People who are in high

asr-001340
01:31:58.960 --> 01:32:02.300
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: school, whose minds

asr-001341
01:32:02.300 --> 01:32:05.140
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: who are in their formative years,

asr-001342
01:32:05.140 --> 01:32:07.200
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: can be able to absorb the ideas

asr-001343
01:32:07.200 --> 01:32:10.660
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: of fighting corruption very early.

asr-001344
01:32:10.660 --> 01:32:12.940
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It has to start, I mean,

asr-001345
01:32:12.940 --> 01:32:14.940
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor, if we can do this as a program

asr-001346
01:32:14.940 --> 01:32:17.580
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: in our educational system,

asr-001347
01:32:17.580 --> 01:32:20.980
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think we would really be a better country.

asr-001348
01:32:20.980 --> 01:32:23.440
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's something that has to start from the youth.

asr-001349
01:32:23.440 --> 01:32:27.580
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's like when we marvel at the Japanese children

asr-001350
01:32:27.580 --> 01:32:28.960
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: walking to school,

asr-001351
01:32:28.960 --> 01:32:33.040
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: unaccompanied by parents without any assistance,

asr-001352
01:32:33.040 --> 01:32:35.500
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because the culture has been created to do that.

asr-001353
01:32:35.500 --> 01:32:37.740
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's something that we can create in our country

asr-001354
01:32:37.740 --> 01:32:42.900
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: to start them young in trying to fight corruption

asr-001355
01:32:42.900 --> 01:32:45.780
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and to be able to know the concept of corruption

asr-001356
01:32:45.780 --> 01:32:47.680
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: as a bad concept, Your Honor.

asr-001357
01:32:48.940 --> 01:32:50.980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you for that, Ombudsman.

asr-001358
01:32:50.980 --> 01:32:52.540
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I really support that.

asr-001359
01:32:52.540 --> 01:32:56.040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: If we can open the eyes and minds of our students

asr-001360
01:32:56.040 --> 01:32:58.840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: in not being in integrity,

asr-001361
01:32:58.960 --> 01:32:59.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: and fighting corruption,

asr-001362
01:32:59.960 --> 01:33:04.080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I think that is the best direction.

asr-001363
01:33:04.080 --> 01:33:09.280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And is this program directed towards that?

asr-001364
01:33:09.280 --> 01:33:11.080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yung mga sa mga bata?

asr-001365
01:33:11.080 --> 01:33:14.200
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001366
01:33:14.200 --> 01:33:16.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Actually, meron akong anecdote.

asr-001367
01:33:16.200 --> 01:33:17.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Nakwento ko ito sa ating chairman eh.

asr-001368
01:33:17.960 --> 01:33:21.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pag may mga lumalapit sa akin

asr-001369
01:33:21.600 --> 01:33:25.240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: humihingi ng job recommendation sa gobyerno,

asr-001370
01:33:25.240 --> 01:33:28.080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: ang pinipili nila kaagad customs.

asr-001371
01:33:28.080 --> 01:33:28.880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: No.

asr-001372
01:33:28.880 --> 01:33:29.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Halos lahat.

asr-001373
01:33:29.440 --> 01:33:30.080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Sabi ko sa inyo, halos lahat

asr-001374
01:33:30.080 --> 01:33:34.120
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: ng recommendation customs.

asr-001375
01:33:34.120 --> 01:33:36.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But the recommendation is for the wrong reason.

asr-001376
01:33:36.400 --> 01:33:42.360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And I made that example because itong mga batang ito na naghahanap ng trabaho,

asr-001377
01:33:42.360 --> 01:33:44.160
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: wrong reasons yung kanilang iniisip.

asr-001378
01:33:44.160 --> 01:33:45.000
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Bakit customs?

asr-001379
01:33:45.000 --> 01:33:51.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Bakit hindi sa DOST or sa ibang mga agencies?

asr-001380
01:33:51.200 --> 01:33:58.080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So that's why mas maganda kung maaga pa lang eh natuturuan na natin sila.

asr-001381
01:33:58.080 --> 01:33:59.360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yung kultura nila maiba,

asr-001382
01:33:59.360 --> 01:34:01.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: yung kanilang pag-iisip.

asr-001383
01:34:01.400 --> 01:34:04.040
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor, I also encountered the same.

asr-001384
01:34:04.040 --> 01:34:10.120
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I had the same experience as somebody working for government.

asr-001385
01:34:10.120 --> 01:34:14.920
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Not only customs, but immigration is another target for many of them.

asr-001386
01:34:14.920 --> 01:34:17.560
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: LTO is another target for many of them.

asr-001387
01:34:17.560 --> 01:34:20.760
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: The revenue-generating agencies actually attract a lot of...

asr-001388
01:34:20.760 --> 01:34:22.360
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And BIR, Your Honor.

asr-001389
01:34:22.360 --> 01:34:23.400
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: The BIR.

asr-001390
01:34:23.400 --> 01:34:25.760
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's...

asr-001391
01:34:25.760 --> 01:34:27.400
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But we know that it's possible

asr-001392
01:34:27.400 --> 01:34:28.200
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: to change the

asr-001393
01:34:28.200 --> 01:34:29.320
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: culture.

asr-001394
01:34:29.360 --> 01:34:30.520
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor.

asr-001395
01:34:30.520 --> 01:34:35.400
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think that we have succeeded to a certain extent in the Bureau of Immigration.

asr-001396
01:34:35.400 --> 01:34:38.640
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think we were able to improve it when I was Secretary of Justice.

asr-001397
01:34:38.640 --> 01:34:41.680
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: The way that it's run, the way that people behave themselves,

asr-001398
01:34:41.680 --> 01:34:43.520
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: the way that they comport themselves.

asr-001399
01:34:43.520 --> 01:34:46.600
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think it can be done with the proper leadership, Your Honor.

asr-001400
01:34:46.600 --> 01:34:47.640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you, Mr. Ambudsman.

asr-001401
01:34:47.640 --> 01:34:48.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-001402
01:34:48.960 --> 01:34:50.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: That's it for me.

asr-001403
01:34:50.600 --> 01:34:51.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-001404
01:34:51.480 --> 01:34:55.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siguro we just have a few questions.

asr-001405
01:34:55.000 --> 01:34:55.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator Lacson.

asr-001406
01:34:55.880 --> 01:34:56.200
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yes.

asr-001407
01:34:56.200 --> 01:34:57.480
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Gusto ko lang makuha yung official

asr-001408
01:34:57.480 --> 01:34:58.480
Senator Panfilo Lacson: position ng Ombudsman doon sa...

asr-001409
01:34:58.480 --> 01:34:59.200
Senator Panfilo Lacson: kasi nag-pass kami ng

asr-001410
01:34:59.200 --> 01:35:00.400
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Judiciary Fiscal Autonomy Act.

asr-001411
01:35:00.400 --> 01:35:05.080
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Because we passed the Judiciary Fiscal Autonomy Act.

asr-001412
01:35:05.080 --> 01:35:09.160
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Of course, guaranteed naman talaga sa Constitution yung fiscal autonomy.

asr-001413
01:35:09.160 --> 01:35:11.200
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero ito na-strengthen pa.

asr-001414
01:35:11.200 --> 01:35:16.080
Senator Panfilo Lacson: But again, ano yung official position ninyo if we enact a similar law

asr-001415
01:35:16.080 --> 01:35:24.390
Senator Panfilo Lacson: that mirrors the statutory powers, yung fiscal autonomy ng judiciary?

asr-001416
01:35:24.390 --> 01:35:28.630
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor, we have to...

asr-001417
01:35:28.630 --> 01:35:29.950
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I'm in favor of that, Your Honor.

asr-001418
01:35:29.950 --> 01:35:30.470
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: That the judiciary should

asr-001419
01:35:30.470 --> 01:35:30.870
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: have fiscal autonomy.

asr-001420
01:35:30.870 --> 01:35:32.510
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Before that happens,

asr-001421
01:35:32.510 --> 01:35:37.990
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But before that happens, we have to be able to ask them the tough questions

asr-001422
01:35:37.990 --> 01:35:40.350
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: that have to be answered, Your Honor.

asr-001423
01:35:40.350 --> 01:35:47.630
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Because if we isolate the judiciary to the point where they become so independent,

asr-001424
01:35:47.630 --> 01:35:51.350
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we might be disappointed.

asr-001425
01:35:51.350 --> 01:35:55.430
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We just want things to be right when we start this, Your Honor.

asr-001426
01:35:55.430 --> 01:35:58.590
Senator Panfilo Lacson: I was referring to the Ombudsman getting the same statutory protection.

asr-001427
01:35:58.590 --> 01:35:59.790
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Magkaroon din kayo,

asr-001428
01:35:59.790 --> 01:36:00.430
Senator Panfilo Lacson: kasi pagka merong fiscal autonomy,

asr-001429
01:36:00.470 --> 01:36:08.990
Senator Panfilo Lacson: yung parang full fiscal autonomy, not just in the implementation,

asr-001430
01:36:08.990 --> 01:36:11.450
Senator Panfilo Lacson: but in the proposal.

asr-001431
01:36:11.450 --> 01:36:17.350
Senator Panfilo Lacson: But I notice also, kasi in spite of the passage of that law,

asr-001432
01:36:17.350 --> 01:36:23.190
Senator Panfilo Lacson: na binibigyan na ng complete fiscal autonomy ang judiciary, nabawasan pa rin sila sa NEP eh.

asr-001433
01:36:23.190 --> 01:36:26.630
Senator Panfilo Lacson: What they proposed. That's why that is an issue that I'd like to raise.

asr-001434
01:36:26.630 --> 01:36:34.490
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Hindi ko lang ni-raise sa DBCC, Mr. President, na bakit nagpasa tayo ng law, may fiscal autonomy,

asr-001435
01:36:34.490 --> 01:36:41.010
Senator Panfilo Lacson: meaning sila na yung nagpe-prepare ng kanilang NEP, at bahala na yung Congress

asr-001436
01:36:41.010 --> 01:36:48.530
Senator Panfilo Lacson: kung anong gagawin by our power of review and oversight, at saka yung pag-review ng National

asr-001437
01:36:48.530 --> 01:36:49.530
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Expenditure Program.

asr-001438
01:36:49.530 --> 01:36:51.530
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kami na magre-review.

asr-001439
01:36:51.530 --> 01:36:56.610
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ang nangyari, I think it was slashed by two billion yata,

asr-001440
01:36:56.610 --> 01:36:59.750
Senator Panfilo Lacson: o three billion eh, as proposed.

asr-001441
01:36:59.750 --> 01:37:01.590
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So where's the fiscal autonomy?

asr-001442
01:37:01.590 --> 01:37:06.650
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So now I'm asking the official position of the Ombudsman, if the same statutory protection

asr-001443
01:37:06.650 --> 01:37:14.670
Senator Panfilo Lacson: sa inyong fiscal autonomy will be granted, para lang ma-enhance yung inyong integrity, independence

asr-001444
01:37:14.670 --> 01:37:17.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: pagdating sa budgeting process.

asr-001445
01:37:17.470 --> 01:37:19.890
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Well, we can use that, Your Honor.

asr-001446
01:37:19.890 --> 01:37:22.470
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It is going to be good for us if we're able to do that.

asr-001447
01:37:22.470 --> 01:37:26.470
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But of course, we will have to be transparent about everything we do.

asr-001448
01:37:26.470 --> 01:37:31.610
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Because it's the last moral compass that we have in government, so it has to be transparent,

asr-001449
01:37:31.610 --> 01:37:32.610
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Your Honor.

asr-001450
01:37:32.610 --> 01:37:33.610
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Mahirap din eh.

asr-001451
01:37:33.610 --> 01:37:37.150
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pag walang fiscal autonomy, at least sa implementation, sa paggastos, okay yun eh.

asr-001452
01:37:37.150 --> 01:37:41.790
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero sa proposal, you're at the mercy of the DBCC.

asr-001453
01:37:41.790 --> 01:37:47.150
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So tulad niyo, nag-propose kayo ng 12 billion plus, 12.8, something like that,

asr-001454
01:37:47.150 --> 01:37:50.650
Senator Panfilo Lacson: pero ang cut 45% eh.

asr-001455
01:37:50.650 --> 01:37:52.550
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So yun lang.

asr-001456
01:37:52.550 --> 01:37:53.550
Senator Panfilo Lacson: I'm just thinking.

asr-001457
01:37:53.550 --> 01:37:54.590
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi binigyan na namin,

asr-001458
01:37:54.590 --> 01:37:55.590
Senator Panfilo Lacson: I think,

asr-001459
01:37:55.590 --> 01:37:56.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: [unclear],

asr-001464
01:38:00.470 --> 01:38:01.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: yun ang

asr-001465
01:38:01.470 --> 01:38:02.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: RA number

asr-001466
01:38:02.470 --> 01:38:03.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: doon sa Judiciary

asr-001467
01:38:03.470 --> 01:38:04.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Fiscal Autonomy

asr-001468
01:38:04.470 --> 01:38:05.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Act.

asr-001469
01:38:05.470 --> 01:38:06.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So ang

asr-001470
01:38:06.470 --> 01:38:07.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: official

asr-001471
01:38:07.470 --> 01:38:08.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: position ninyo is

asr-001472
01:38:08.470 --> 01:38:09.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: for that?

asr-001473
01:38:09.470 --> 01:38:10.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yeah.

asr-001474
01:38:10.470 --> 01:38:11.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-001475
01:38:11.470 --> 01:38:12.470
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes.

asr-001476
01:38:12.470 --> 01:38:13.470
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-001477
01:38:13.470 --> 01:38:18.390
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator Lacson, actually, the Office of the Ombudsman complies itong budget, 2027,

asr-001478
01:38:18.390 --> 01:38:25.610
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: with the requirement under Section 38 of RA 6770, which states that

asr-001479
01:38:25.610 --> 01:38:27.610
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the Office of the Ombudsman

asr-001480
01:38:27.610 --> 01:38:29.930
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: shall enjoy fiscal autonomy

asr-001481
01:38:29.930 --> 01:38:31.670
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: in its appropriations. We can just

asr-001482
01:38:31.670 --> 01:38:33.470
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: enhance, no?

asr-001483
01:38:33.470 --> 01:38:34.550
Senator Panfilo Lacson: That's already in the Constitution, I think

asr-001484
01:38:34.550 --> 01:38:36.730
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Article XI?

asr-001485
01:38:38.250 --> 01:38:38.970
Senator Panfilo Lacson: That's correct.

asr-001486
01:38:39.350 --> 01:38:40.670
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Section 14 ba yan? Anyway,

asr-001487
01:38:41.310 --> 01:38:43.930
Senator Panfilo Lacson: nandiyan na yun, pero ang nire-refer ko

asr-001488
01:38:43.930 --> 01:38:44.910
Senator Panfilo Lacson: sa proposal,

asr-001489
01:38:45.690 --> 01:38:47.650
Senator Panfilo Lacson: kasi yung fiscal autonomy nila is in

asr-001490
01:38:47.650 --> 01:38:49.550
Senator Panfilo Lacson: the implementation, sa execution ng

asr-001491
01:38:49.550 --> 01:38:52.150
Senator Panfilo Lacson: budget, pero hindi covered yung proposal.

asr-001492
01:38:52.450 --> 01:38:53.650
Senator Panfilo Lacson: But then I'm wondering,

asr-001493
01:38:53.650 --> 01:38:55.290
Senator Panfilo Lacson: meron na nga sa Judiciary,

asr-001494
01:38:55.410 --> 01:38:57.450
Senator Panfilo Lacson: kinat pa rin ng DBCC.

asr-001495
01:38:58.050 --> 01:38:59.670
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So where's the fiscal autonomy

asr-001496
01:38:59.670 --> 01:39:02.250
Senator Panfilo Lacson: doon sa proposal? Dapat Congress

asr-001497
01:39:02.250 --> 01:39:03.050
Senator Panfilo Lacson: na yung magre-review.

asr-001498
01:39:03.650 --> 01:39:04.790
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Hindi na kayo dadaan sa

asr-001499
01:39:04.790 --> 01:39:07.670
Senator Panfilo Lacson: budget call. You'll still be

asr-001500
01:39:07.670 --> 01:39:09.370
Senator Panfilo Lacson: reporting to the DBCC

asr-001501
01:39:09.370 --> 01:39:11.730
Senator Panfilo Lacson: for processing or

asr-001502
01:39:11.730 --> 01:39:13.550
Senator Panfilo Lacson: vetting. So, anyway,

asr-001503
01:39:13.830 --> 01:39:15.730
Senator Panfilo Lacson: May power naman yung Congress.

asr-001504
01:39:15.730 --> 01:39:17.790
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kami naman yung so-called power of the purse,

asr-001505
01:39:17.890 --> 01:39:18.310
Senator Panfilo Lacson: maski hindi...

asr-001506
01:39:20.550 --> 01:39:21.430
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi hindi naman kami

asr-001507
01:39:21.430 --> 01:39:22.230
Senator Panfilo Lacson: nag-i-implement eh.

asr-001508
01:39:23.150 --> 01:39:23.590
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Sorry.

asr-001509
01:39:23.650 --> 01:39:25.330
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Probably, a test would be

asr-001510
01:39:25.330 --> 01:39:26.350
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: absorptive capacity.

asr-001511
01:39:27.130 --> 01:39:29.510
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: The capacity to

asr-001512
01:39:29.510 --> 01:39:31.510
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: spend the money has to be

asr-001513
01:39:31.510 --> 01:39:33.470
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: there when we approve these

asr-001514
01:39:33.470 --> 01:39:35.050
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: things. Because I think that's the

asr-001515
01:39:35.050 --> 01:39:37.310
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: if I put my mind in the

asr-001516
01:39:37.310 --> 01:39:39.010
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: myself in the seat of the executive,

asr-001517
01:39:39.590 --> 01:39:41.330
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: it's just clearly wasting

asr-001518
01:39:41.330 --> 01:39:43.410
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: resources if they ask for too much

asr-001519
01:39:43.410 --> 01:39:44.850
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and they're not able to spend it, Your Honor.

asr-001520
01:39:48.720 --> 01:39:49.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator

asr-001521
01:39:49.160 --> 01:39:50.720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: President Pro Temp?

asr-001522
01:39:51.060 --> 01:39:52.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay na, Senator Lacson?

asr-001523
01:39:53.020 --> 01:39:54.100
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Senate President Pro Tempore,

asr-001524
01:39:54.100 --> 01:39:55.420
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: If you're

asr-001525
01:39:55.440 --> 01:39:58.140
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: if you're done with that topic

asr-001526
01:39:58.140 --> 01:40:00.300
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: before, before we move

asr-001527
01:40:00.300 --> 01:40:02.100
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: for the approval of the budget of

asr-001528
01:40:02.100 --> 01:40:04.120
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: the Ombudsman, subject, of

asr-001529
01:40:04.120 --> 01:40:05.460
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: course, to the amendments that are

asr-001530
01:40:05.460 --> 01:40:06.460
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: being proposed.

asr-001531
01:40:07.380 --> 01:40:09.120
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Just out of curiosity,

asr-001532
01:40:11.160 --> 01:40:13.080
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: you might not be aware, but

asr-001533
01:40:13.080 --> 01:40:14.460
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I watch the two of you every

asr-001534
01:40:14.460 --> 01:40:15.460
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Saturday.

asr-001535
01:40:16.660 --> 01:40:18.540
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And my wife

asr-001536
01:40:18.540 --> 01:40:20.520
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: is a fan of your, what

asr-001537
01:40:20.520 --> 01:40:22.080
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: do you call that, executive session?

asr-001538
01:40:22.080 --> 01:40:23.100
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: No.

asr-001539
01:40:23.100 --> 01:40:25.380
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: One time you were quoted

asr-001540
01:40:25.440 --> 01:40:27.800
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: to say that ang tindi ng corruption

asr-001541
01:40:27.800 --> 01:40:29.140
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: sa basura ng LGU.

asr-001542
01:40:29.140 --> 01:40:39.820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: How do they do that? I'm interested because

asr-001543
01:40:39.820 --> 01:40:42.040
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I have friends in the LGU

asr-001544
01:40:42.040 --> 01:40:44.660
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: that are interested to find out how they

asr-001545
01:40:45.520 --> 01:40:45.980
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: will be able to stop it.

asr-001546
01:40:45.980 --> 01:40:47.960
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Mr. Ombudsman?

asr-001547
01:40:47.960 --> 01:40:51.920
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: or stop it with the Ombudsman.

asr-001548
01:40:51.920 --> 01:40:54.100
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor, may mga character tayo sa society

asr-001549
01:40:54.100 --> 01:40:57.580
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: na basura king eh. The big haulers are basura kings, Your Honor.

asr-001550
01:40:58.080 --> 01:41:03.400
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And they're here in Manila, in Metro Manila, in Manila, City of Manila, everywhere.

asr-001551
01:41:04.320 --> 01:41:12.680
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And the tragedy, Your Honor, is that the work of the DENR is never started or finished

asr-001552
01:41:12.680 --> 01:41:17.780
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because the garbage hauling begins with local government and nothing is followed.

asr-001553
01:41:19.280 --> 01:41:22.280
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Segregation, proper sanitary landfills.

asr-001554
01:41:22.280 --> 01:41:25.860
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Everything becomes a dump, Your Honor.

asr-001555
01:41:26.280 --> 01:41:26.960
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: That's the problem.

asr-001556
01:41:28.860 --> 01:41:35.240
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But probably the DNR should have a bigger hand in it so that things will be better.

asr-001557
01:41:35.240 --> 01:41:44.220
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But as long as what they do is to dump the trash in specific places that they are able to contract with,

asr-001558
01:41:46.740 --> 01:41:48.220
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: it's big money for them, Your Honor.

asr-001559
01:41:48.700 --> 01:41:53.720
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Because the budgets for basura is so big that

asr-001560
01:41:53.720 --> 01:41:58.580
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: it can blind a lot of people into just making money out of it.

asr-001561
01:41:59.100 --> 01:42:02.380
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think that for those who have been in politics for a long time,

asr-001562
01:42:02.720 --> 01:42:03.880
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we've seen it happen, Your Honor.

asr-001563
01:42:04.460 --> 01:42:07.420
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: These basura kings are around the metropolis, Your Honor.

asr-001564
01:42:08.700 --> 01:42:10.480
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And also nationwide.

asr-001565
01:42:11.440 --> 01:42:12.260
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Nationwide, Your Honor.

asr-001566
01:42:14.600 --> 01:42:18.600
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's actually, when I started talking about this basura,

asr-001567
01:42:19.160 --> 01:42:23.540
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think it touched a lot of raw nerves because we know it to be true, I think.

asr-001568
01:42:23.720 --> 01:42:24.680
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We know it to be true, Your Honor.

asr-001569
01:42:25.500 --> 01:42:36.320
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And would you have anyone in the Ombudsman that would give some local government officials

asr-001570
01:42:36.320 --> 01:42:45.400
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: how they are going about the pattern and saan kumikita, saan natataga yung mga kababayan natin?

asr-001571
01:42:46.200 --> 01:42:48.800
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We will create a special investigative team for this, Your Honor.

asr-001572
01:42:49.200 --> 01:42:49.800
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We will do it.

asr-001573
01:42:49.940 --> 01:42:51.960
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: All right. Thank you very much. Thank you for that.

asr-001574
01:42:51.960 --> 01:42:52.620
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you.

asr-001575
01:42:52.620 --> 01:42:53.600
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Napag-usapan niyong basura.

asr-001576
01:42:53.720 --> 01:42:55.880
Senator Panfilo Lacson: I was tempted to inquire about the Taguig.

asr-001577
01:42:57.840 --> 01:43:00.700
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Baka mapagbintangan ako, nagde-demolition job.

asr-001578
01:43:00.760 --> 01:43:07.020
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Anyway, we're quietly but surely assisting the Ombudsman in this regard,

asr-001579
01:43:07.020 --> 01:43:09.740
Senator Panfilo Lacson: kasi I understand the complexity of the problem,

asr-001580
01:43:10.340 --> 01:43:12.780
Senator Panfilo Lacson: yung volume ng mga graft and corruption cases.

asr-001581
01:43:13.140 --> 01:43:15.240
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung office nga lang namin, Mr. Ombudsman,

asr-001582
01:43:16.100 --> 01:43:21.280
Senator Panfilo Lacson: case studies lang ang pinaggugulan namin ng panahon, pero ubos talaga oras namin.

asr-001583
01:43:21.280 --> 01:43:23.700
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Case studies in Bulacan,

asr-001584
01:43:23.840 --> 01:43:26.880
Senator Panfilo Lacson: case studies in Mindoro and in Taguig.

asr-001585
01:43:27.080 --> 01:43:28.520
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Hirap na hirap na yung mga staff.

asr-001586
01:43:28.520 --> 01:43:32.580
Senator Panfilo Lacson: What more na swarmed by so many cases ang Ombudsman,

asr-001587
01:43:32.580 --> 01:43:38.700
Senator Panfilo Lacson: very complex, hindi lang flood control, all sorts of graft and corruption cases.

asr-001588
01:43:39.100 --> 01:43:43.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So that's why we are really very supportive of the efforts of the Ombudsman

asr-001589
01:43:44.400 --> 01:43:49.500
Senator Panfilo Lacson: and in whatever capacity na makatulong kami, like the judicial marshal service,

asr-001590
01:43:49.920 --> 01:43:53.240
Senator Panfilo Lacson: yung fiscal autonomy, etcetera.

asr-001591
01:43:53.240 --> 01:43:53.680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So, he says,

asr-001592
01:43:53.680 --> 01:44:02.100
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So rest assured that the Senate, under the leadership of the Senate President, will be foursquare behind the efforts of the Ombudsman.

asr-001593
01:44:03.000 --> 01:44:03.600
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you, Your Honor.

asr-001594
01:44:05.480 --> 01:44:06.100
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Mr. Chairman.

asr-001595
01:44:07.200 --> 01:44:15.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, before the Senate President, I would like to acknowledge also the presence of our Blue Ribbon Chair, Senator Erwin Tulfo.

asr-001596
01:44:15.780 --> 01:44:16.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, sir, for joining us.

asr-001597
01:44:16.780 --> 01:44:20.040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, just a brief intervention lang.

asr-001598
01:44:20.040 --> 01:44:30.360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I was looking at itong corruption index scores natin, corruption perception index.

asr-001599
01:44:31.200 --> 01:44:45.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And sad to say, in the last three years, bumagsak yung ating ranking, from 144, the lowest rank being the least corrupt.

asr-001600
01:44:45.320 --> 01:44:49.280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: From 144 rank naging 120 rank na tayo.

asr-001601
01:44:50.040 --> 01:45:00.000
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And we're now the third most corrupt in Southeast Asia, next to Myanmar and Cambodia, which are...

asr-001602
01:45:00.000 --> 01:45:02.640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: alam naman natin, are junta states.

asr-001603
01:45:02.920 --> 01:45:12.660
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So there is really a very big challenge for all of us to improve the perception of corruption in our country.

asr-001604
01:45:13.160 --> 01:45:14.340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Apektado tayo lahat eh.

asr-001605
01:45:14.740 --> 01:45:20.180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In fact, one of the reasons bakit mahina ang peso, dahil walang demand sa peso.

asr-001606
01:45:20.640 --> 01:45:22.280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Walang nag-i-invest sa ating bansa.

asr-001607
01:45:23.300 --> 01:45:28.900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasama na dito rin itong, of course, ease of doing business and also the perception of corruption.

asr-001608
01:45:28.900 --> 01:45:32.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So it's really a big challenge for all of us.

asr-001609
01:45:33.120 --> 01:45:36.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And that is why I second the statement of Senator Lacson na

asr-001610
01:45:36.580 --> 01:45:42.140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: whatever we can do to help the Ombudsman, even the judiciary, to fight corruption, we will do it.

asr-001611
01:45:42.820 --> 01:45:52.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because it affects our country, it affects our OFWs, it affects even the most ordinary Filipino.

asr-001612
01:45:52.860 --> 01:45:55.300
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So kailangan talaga magtulong-tulong tayo diyan.

asr-001613
01:45:56.640 --> 01:45:57.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, sir.

asr-001614
01:45:58.900 --> 01:46:03.120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Our Blue Ribbon Chair is also here.

asr-001615
01:46:03.280 --> 01:46:04.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you for joining us.

asr-001616
01:46:04.540 --> 01:46:06.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator Erwin Tulfo, you now have the floor.

asr-001617
01:46:12.460 --> 01:46:16.240
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Anyway, I don't know, Mr. Chair, if this was already asked.

asr-001618
01:46:16.240 --> 01:46:18.700
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ito lang po nakita ko, napansin kanina dito.

asr-001619
01:46:19.340 --> 01:46:22.700
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Itong total number of authorized positions, Mr. Chair.

asr-001620
01:46:23.440 --> 01:46:28.240
Senator Erwin Tulfo: 2,439 po nire-request po ng authorized positions.

asr-001621
01:46:28.900 --> 01:46:33.120
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Pero ang filled positions lamang ay 1,192.

asr-001622
01:46:33.400 --> 01:46:43.040
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Dito po sa 2,439, Mr. Chair, Ombudsman, karamihan po ba nito ay mga investigators po ninyo?

asr-001623
01:46:43.300 --> 01:46:44.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: You would need lawyers?

asr-001624
01:46:46.040 --> 01:46:48.100
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Sa anong mga positions po ito?

asr-001625
01:46:48.820 --> 01:46:52.080
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We will need more lawyers and technical investigators, Your Honor.

asr-001626
01:46:52.420 --> 01:46:58.120
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Engineers who can educate us about infrastructure fraud, infrastructure corruption.

asr-001627
01:46:58.900 --> 01:47:05.500
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And other specialists, Your Honor, who are good at investigating different kinds of crimes, Your Honor.

asr-001628
01:47:06.160 --> 01:47:08.160
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Mga normal positions po ito.

asr-001629
01:47:08.160 --> 01:47:09.400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I mean regular po.

asr-001630
01:47:09.920 --> 01:47:11.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Regular positions po ito.

asr-001631
01:47:11.500 --> 01:47:17.600
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Hindi po ito yung basta-bastang mga contractual employees.

asr-001632
01:47:17.920 --> 01:47:18.200
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor.

asr-001633
01:47:18.300 --> 01:47:19.460
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: They are plantilla positions.

asr-001634
01:47:19.760 --> 01:47:20.220
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Plantilla positions.

asr-001635
01:47:20.240 --> 01:47:20.620
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001636
01:47:20.840 --> 01:47:21.180
Senator Erwin Tulfo: All right.

asr-001637
01:47:21.300 --> 01:47:21.820
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you po.

asr-001638
01:47:22.200 --> 01:47:22.940
Senator Erwin Tulfo: That's all, Mr. Chair.

asr-001639
01:47:23.640 --> 01:47:26.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Tulfo.

asr-001640
01:47:26.680 --> 01:47:27.040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Likewise.

asr-001641
01:47:27.040 --> 01:47:29.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Isang tanong na lang.

asr-001642
01:47:29.340 --> 01:47:34.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung tungkol sa Resident Ombudsman Program, what is the current status of the Resident Ombudsman Program,

asr-001643
01:47:34.540 --> 01:47:39.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: including the number of active resident ombudsmen, their deployment across agencies,

asr-001644
01:47:39.700 --> 01:47:43.860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and the key accomplishments or challenges encountered recently?

asr-001645
01:47:44.320 --> 01:47:47.560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siguro, Assistant Ombudsman Bonoan, please.

asr-001646
01:47:48.080 --> 01:47:54.280
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: Your Honor, actually, during this administration, we have reactivated the Bureau of the Resident Ombudsman,

asr-001647
01:47:54.280 --> 01:47:55.840
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: which had remained inactive.

asr-001648
01:47:55.840 --> 01:47:57.700
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: the last several years.

asr-001649
01:47:58.360 --> 01:48:07.080
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: So, as of today, we have hired an additional 10 lawyers to complement our Bureau of Resident Ombudsman.

asr-001650
01:48:07.280 --> 01:48:15.120
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: And we have plans, sir, after conducting the proper training, of fielding them out in different agencies,

asr-001651
01:48:15.340 --> 01:48:24.820
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: particularly the high revenue generating agencies, sir, to investigate and collect complaints from therein.

asr-001652
01:48:25.200 --> 01:48:25.820
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: Your Honor.

asr-001653
01:48:25.840 --> 01:48:26.380
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: Thank you.

asr-001654
01:48:26.800 --> 01:48:27.320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay, thank you.

asr-001655
01:48:27.840 --> 01:48:33.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Anyway, before we close, if there are no more questions or queries from our colleagues.

asr-001656
01:48:34.320 --> 01:48:35.840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, Senate President Pro Tempore.

asr-001657
01:48:36.440 --> 01:48:37.200
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-001658
01:48:37.360 --> 01:48:44.140
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I move that we submit and approve the budget of the Ombudsman, together with the proposed amendments.

asr-001659
01:48:44.440 --> 01:48:45.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I second the motion.

asr-001660
01:48:46.080 --> 01:48:50.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Since it has been moved by our Senate President Pro Tempore and seconded,

asr-001661
01:48:50.640 --> 01:48:55.720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the budget of the Office of the Ombudsman is now deemed submitted for the plenary's consideration,

asr-001662
01:48:55.840 --> 01:48:59.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: subject to the discussion and submission of documents requested.

asr-001663
01:48:59.600 --> 01:49:05.260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you very much, gentlemen, Ombudsman, and to all the rest of the officials of the Office of the Ombudsman.

asr-001664
01:49:05.360 --> 01:49:05.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-001665
01:49:06.080 --> 01:49:07.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: This briefing is hereby suspended.

asr-001666
01:49:08.280 --> 01:49:08.740
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Thank you.

asr-001667
01:49:08.820 --> 01:49:09.280
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Thank you, sir.

